commit 9390f078e9ea967afc8a96b11e65595ca00dcfa4
Author: zhangyi101 <zhangyi101@xiaomi.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 17:36:32 2026 +0800

    media: fix stale stream fd on async reset

    VELAPLATFO-97454

    The async reset path never released the chain's local stream state, so
    after a buffer or direct reset the recorder kept chain->fd open and a
    late read callback could close a descriptor already reused by the next
    prepare. The read error path had the same defect: it closed the fd but
    left it set in the chain.

    Release the stream through the common close handler on read error, and
    run the same teardown as stop in the uv reset paths.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Change-Id: Ie38d41bd3869245f512ac2e29a68c5220ea494c9
    Signed-off-by: zhangyi101 <zhangyi101@xiaomi.com>

